--- body ---
## Context

The `method` field in `measurements.jsonl` is the most load-bearing
name in the project — every downstream plot, table, and report section
reads it. Design decision (2026-04-24): clean separation of two axes:

- `method` — information access mode (where does the model's knowledge
  come from?). Model-agnostic. No prompt content encoded here.
- `prompt_version` (in `method_params`) — which prompt was used.
  Already present in the schema; currently underused (`"derived"`).

`rag` and `rag_livesearch` are both retrieval-augmented; the axis is
how the corpus was assembled: curated (Zotero PDFs) vs dynamic (live
Tavily search). `rag_livesearch` names the mechanism, not just the
source.

## Confirmed vocabulary

| Current method | New method     | prompt_version |
|----------------|----------------|----------------|
| single         | direct         | extract        |
| frontier       | direct         | complete       |
| frontier_scenarios | direct     | scenarios      |
| web            | rag_livesearch | extract        |
| rag            | rag            | extract        |
| decomposed     | rag            | per_fuel       |
| sourced        | rag            | cited          |
| multiturn      | multiturn      | extract        |
| verification   | verification   | —              |
| frontier_skill | DELETE         | DELETE         |

Ablation runs currently write `prompt_version: "derived"`. Encoding:
mirror the sweep condition label directly — `"ablation_base"`,
`"ablation_composite"`, `"ablation_persona"`, `"ablation_no_persona"`,
etc. The harness derives this from the sweep name or module list.
No new vocabulary needed; the sweep IDs are already systematic.

## Actions

1. Count occurrences by current method in `measurements.jsonl` to
   surface migration surface area before writing any code.
2. Delete `frontier_skill` data:
   - Remove `[sweeps.frontier_skill]` from `experiments.toml`.
   - `git rm -r experiments/qualitative/skill_plans/` (if it exists).
   - Purge `measurements.jsonl` entries whose `result_file` points to
     `qualitative/skill_plans/`.
3. Write `scripts/migrate_method_values.py` — idempotent migration:
   rewrites `measurements.jsonl` in place applying the table above,
   adding `prompt_version` to `method_params` where missing.
4. Update `harness.py` (and all `query_*.py` writers) to emit the new
   `method` and `prompt_version` values for future runs.
5. Update all readers: `evaluate.py`, `measurements.py`,
   `plot_*.py`, `tabulate_*.py` — any code that matches on method
   strings. Compound filters (`method == "rag" AND prompt_version ==
   "per_fuel"`) replace bare `method == "decomposed"` guards.
6. Run `make test` green.
7. Two commits: (a) migration script + data, (b) code changes.

## Exit criteria

- `measurements.jsonl` contains no old method values.
- `harness.py` and all query runners emit new method + prompt_version.
- All readers updated; `make test` green.
- Vocabulary table committed as a comment in `harness.py`.
- `frontier_skill` fully purged.
- Unblocks 0121, 0124.
